   "text": "I read the structure in sections and wrote each one as SMILES, then joined them.\n\n- **Core:** a pyrido[4,3-d]pyrimidine. Position 4 carries the Boc-protected 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane through its N3. Position 8 carries F. Position 2 carries an O\u2013CH2 link to the pyrrolidine. Position 7 carries the naphthyl group.\n- **Naphthyl group:** 8-ethynyl-7-fluoro with a MOM-protected hydroxyl (OCH2OCH3) at position 3.\n- **Pyrrolidine:** N-methyl, with CH2O groups at C2 and C5. One CH2 is on a wedge and the other on a hash.\n- **Right-hand side:** the C5 CH2O is a carbamate (OC(=O)N) onto a piperazine. The piperazine's other nitrogen is bonded to the aromatic ring of an isoindolinone. The isoindolinone N is bonded to the glutarimide (2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl). That glutarimide stereocentre is drawn plain, so it has no stereo label.\n- **Stereochemistry:** I worked out both pyrrolidine centres from the wedge and hash, and both come out as @@ in the SMILES order used.\n\nI checked the SMILES for valid ring closures and matched it atom by atom against the drawing.\n\nSMILES: COCOc1cc(-c2ncc3c(N4CC5CCC(C4)N5C(=O)OC(C)(C)C)nc(OC[C@@H]4CC[C@@H](COC(=O)N5CCN(CC5)c5ccc6C(=O)N(C7CCC(=O)NC7=O)Cc6c5)N4C)nc3c2F)c2c(C#C)c(F)ccc2c1"
